    "kin-peoples-union": {"value":2,"rationale":"Akçura's 1904 essay proposes a political nation uniting all Turks 'dispersed in eastern Europe and a large part of Asia' who share race, language and customs, and Zenkovsky calls it the gospel of Pan-Turkism; Atsız makes the liberation of Turks outside Turkey the content of Turanism. The OTS pursues integration by cooperation, but the defining aim in the scholarship is unity across borders.","sources":["s1","s4","s3"]},
