    "language-defines-nation": {"value":1,"rationale":"Gökalp defines the nation by shared language, education and culture and asks whether Oghuz Turks in Turkey, Azerbaijan and Iran can be called different nations when their language and culture are the same; Akçura and Gasprinski likewise unite Turks by language. Religion is one element in Gökalp's list, not a limit.","sources":["s2","s1","s4"]},
