  "notes": "Searched, theme by theme, the main corpus reachable: Akçura's essay, Berkes's Gökalp essays (programme, nation, language, religion, politics, economy), Atsız's articles, Zenkovsky on Gasprinski and the Russian Turks, the Nine Lights text and OTS declarations. Strands: Gasprinski and the Tatar liberals sought cultural unity inside Russia and a constitutional order; Akçura a political Turkic nation; Gökalp a cultural, non-racial nation that became Turkey-focused after 1918 (Berkes: he dismissed Turan then); Atsız a racial Turanism claiming Turkic lands; the OTS cooperation that respects borders. Positions held by one thinker only (women's equality, democracy, state economy, leader and party rule) are null. Not reached: the Turkic World Vision 2040 and the Nakhchivan agreement (OTS site 403 and 401), Landau, Heyd and Hostler (lending copies only), Gökalp's two Turan essays (not in the Berkes selection), Togan's memoirs (not searched in depth)."
}
